# Project Rules

## Forms

- Use React Hook Form for all forms.
- Use Zod for schema-based validation.
- Avoid manual form validation when a schema can be used.

## Components

- Prefer reusable components over duplicated JSX.
- Keep components focused on a single responsibility.
- Avoid unnecessary inline styles.

## Accessibility

- Every input must have an associated label.
- Use aria-invalid and aria-describedby for validation errors.
- Ensure keyboard accessibility for interactive elements.

## Verification

- Review the AI's implementation plan before approving code generation.
- Run npm run lint before committing changes.
- Run npm run build before committing changes.
- Fix verification failures instead of bypassing them.

## Testing

- Add unit tests for new interactive components.
- Verify validation logic through automated tests whenever possible.